THOUGHT: The transient iterator fields are lazily initialized in iterator() methods, but NullAway wants them non-null on all constructor paths. Safest is to eagerly initialize them in the main constructor after keyTable/valueTable are set, preserving existing lazy-reset behavior. I’ll edit the constructor to assign new Entries/Values/Keys to entries1/entries2/values1/values2/keys1/keys2, then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '103,115s@^\(  public ObjectFloatMap(int initialCapacity, float loadFactor) {\)@\1
    entries1 = new Entries<>(this);
    entries2 = new Entries<>(this);
    values1 = new Values(this);
    values2 = new Values(this);
    keys1 = new Keys<>(this);
    keys2 = new Keys<>(this);@' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/ObjectFloatMap.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

